 "capsule": "Moghulistan was the Turco-Mongol successor khanate that broke from the Chagatai ulus in 1347, when the Dughlat amir Bulaji installed the Chagatayid Tughlugh Timur as khan over the nomadic tribes of the Ili region and the Tarim Basin oasis towns. Tughlugh Timur's 1354 conversion to Islam and his 1360-61 invasions of Transoxiana briefly reunited the eastern and western Chagatai lands before his 1363 death plunged the khanate into decades of Dughlat-dominated civil war. Later khans such as Yunus, Mahmud, and Ahmad Alaq ruled a still largely nomadic Moghulistan from bases like Tashkent and Aksu, resisting the Timurids, Oirats, and Uzbek Shaybanids until the realm's final division around 1514-16 into the Yarkent and Turfan khanates.",
